From: Lunduke Journal <bryan@lunduke.com>
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] screen: do not dereference NULL when a wide glyph lands in the last column

REP (CSI Ps b) repeats the last printed character without the wrap check that normal text
gets, so repeating a double-width character can put it in the last column. putglyph() then
marks the right half with getcell(row, cols)->chars[0] = -1. getcell() returns NULL for a
column off the screen, so this is a NULL dereference (UBSan: screen.c:190:46 "member access
within null pointer of type 'ScreenCell'"; a crash without sanitizers). Reproducer:
tests/data/fuzz/crash-46ca723d-libvterm-rep.bin (found by tools/fuzz/vterm_fuzz);
test: tests/libvterm_rep_test.cpp.

Fix: skip right-half cells that are off the screen and clip the damage rectangle to the
screen width. Inputs that do not reach this case produce exactly what stock 0.3.3 produces.
Vim's bundled libvterm uses the same break-on-NULL check in this loop.

Local patch for Lunduke Terminal; not sent upstream.

--- a/src/screen.c
+++ b/src/screen.c
@@ -186,8 +186,14 @@
   if(i < VTERM_MAX_CHARS_PER_CELL)
     cell->chars[i] = 0;
 
-  for(int col = 1; col < info->width; col++)
-    getcell(screen, pos.row, pos.col + col)->chars[0] = (uint32_t)-1;
+  for(int col = 1; col < info->width; col++) {
+    ScreenCell *gap = getcell(screen, pos.row, pos.col + col);
+    if(!gap)
+      /* A wide glyph in the last column (REP repeating a wide character at the right margin):
+       * its right half would be off the screen, where getcell() returns NULL. */
+      break;
+    gap->chars[0] = (uint32_t)-1;
+  }
 
   VTermRect rect = {
     .start_row = pos.row,
@@ -195,6 +201,8 @@
     .start_col = pos.col,
     .end_col   = pos.col+info->width,
   };
+  if(rect.end_col > screen->cols)
+    rect.end_col = screen->cols;
 
   cell->pen.protected_cell = info->protected_cell;
   cell->pen.dwl            = info->dwl;
